  "sourceDerivedFindings": [
    "FileObject native smartblock value is 0x215 (533); generic File object layout is 6. Specialized image/audio/video/pdf layouts are distinct.",
    "FileInfo carries fileId and repeated path/key encryptionKeys. Modern detail TargetObjectID is the captured head; it is not payload fileId.",
    "The original constructor always creates smartblock/header/title/featuredRelations, then file/info/description/fileExt plus nonzero sizeInBytes/origin/importType/addedDate relation blocks. WithAllBlocksEditsRestricted sets read=false and edit/remove/drag/dropOn=true.",
    "The generated self file block has targetObjectId equal to its own head, name/MIME/size/addedAt from details, Type File=1, State Done=2, Style Auto=0, empty legacy hash. Its reference row is required, not an arbitrary referring-document file block.",
    "Native raw JSON uses OrigName=true, EmitDefaults=true, EnumsAsInts=true. File size and addedAt are protobuf int64 JSON strings; fileInfo encryption entries and unknown protobuf bytes remain exact source evidence.",
    "Variant detail arrays are generated in parallel; indexed generic file details include name without extension, fileExt, MIME, size, added/modified times and FileId. AdditionalDetails and later edits can alter them, so constructor shape alone is not positive capture admission.",
    "All complete snapshots, native trees, variant metadata/payload and original private metadata must remain in the archive; an attachment upload does not activate the File Type or migrate native history."
  ],
